          "final_text_tail": "odes.Const`, `nodes.Name`, simple `nodes.Call` (with `nodes.Name` callee), `nodes.Getattr`, `nodes.Filter`, and `nodes.Test`.\n  - Disallowed expression types: `nodes.TemplateData`, `nodes.Output`, complex calls, and nested data structures.\n\n#### Task 2: Conditional Translation Rendering Extension\n- Added [`ConditionalI18nExtension`](file:///private/var/folders/3q/2m8v425s7p39t7qxjp0kcdw80000gn/T/parbench-host-6c7kto6m/repo/src/jinja2/ext.py#L636) registering `tags = {\"ctrans\"}` and module-level alias `conditional_i18n = ConditionalI18nExtension`.\n- Implemented `parse()`, `_parse_block()`, `_trim_whitespace()`, and `_make_conditional_node()` supporting:\n  - Optional commas anywhere in the header (e.g. `{% ctrans cond, name %}` or `{% ctrans cond name %}`).\n  - Singular translatable block, optional `{% pluralize [var] %}` block, and mandatory `{% fallback %}` block.\n  - `trimmed` and `notrimmed` modifiers applied to singular, plural, and fallback blocks, respecting `ext.i18n.trimmed` policy.\n  - AST generation with `nodes.If` executing `gettext`/`ngettext` translations on the true branch and rendering fallback content directly with variable substitution on the false branch.\n  - Support for both new-style gettext formatting and old-style formatting with `nodes.MarkSafeIfAutoescape`.\n  - Error handling for missing fallback block (`TemplateSyntaxError`), unclosed conditional translation blocks (`TemplateSyntaxError`), and duplicate variable definitions (`TemplateAssertionError`).\n",
